Key distinction. The AI module is QM (Quality Management, unrated) under ISO 26262. The safety authority is developed to ASIL D. The independence requirement means the safety authority must be implemented in a separate execution domain (e.g., a separate core or a certified microcontroller) and must not share memory or timing resources with the AI module. For AI SoCs developed as SEooC, the trusted statement must simultaneously specify the certification or evaluation object, covered functions and versions, usage assumptions, external safety mechanisms, and the final evidence scope.

