13. Toy Instantiation

13.1 System Description

Consider a double integrator with battery dynamics:

\ddot{x} = u, \qquad E_{t+1} = E_t - \|u_t\|^2,

with state x \in \mathbb{R}^2, control u \in \mathbb{R}, safety constraint h(x) = x_{\max} - \|x\| \geq 0, and resource constraint E_t \geq E_{\min}.

The augmented state is \tilde{x} = (x, E). The resource-aware viability kernel \mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{res}} shrinks relative to the classical viability kernel \mathcal{K} as E decreases. Figure 1 illustrates this shrinkage for a 2D system.

13.2 Demonstration of Monotonicity

For this system, the throughput form \rho(u) = u yields

\rho_{\max}(\Sigma, E) = \sup \{ u : u \in \mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\Sigma, E) \}.

As \Sigma increases, \rho_{\max} decreases. As E decreases, \rho_{\max} decreases. This confirms Design Axiom D1 in the monotone regime.

13.3 CARe vs. Exact HJ

For n=2, exact HJ reachability is tractable and serves as the ground truth. CARe with a neural network approximation achieves \epsilon-close reachable sets with SMT-certified error bounds, demonstrating the viability of the certified approximation approach.

