Appendix G: Toy Instantiation

G.1 System Description

Consider a double integrator with battery dynamics:

\ddot{x} = u, \qquad E_{t+1} = E_t - \|u_t\|^2,

with state x \in \mathbb{R}^2, control u \in \mathbb{R}, safety constraint h(x) = x_{\max} - \|x\| \geq 0, and resource constraint E_t \geq E_{\min}.

G.2 Augmented State and Viability Kernel

The augmented state is \tilde{x} = (x, E). The resource-aware viability kernel \mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{res}} is computed via the two-stage approximation:

Stage 1: Compute the classical viability kernel \mathcal{K} for the double integrator with safety constraint h(x) \geq 0.

Stage 2: For each E, compute the reachable set of the resource dynamics and intersect with \mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{adm}}.

G.3 Numerical Example (2D)

For x \in \mathbb{R}^2 and E \in \mathbb{R}, the classical viability kernel \mathcal{K} is a subset of \mathbb{R}^2. The resource-aware viability kernel \mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{res}} is a subset of \mathbb{R}^3. The projection of \mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{res}} onto \mathbb{R}^2 shrinks as E decreases. Figure G.1 illustrates this shrinkage.

