G.4 Monotonicity Demonstration

For this system, the throughput form \rho(u) = u yields

\rho_{\max}(\Sigma, E) = \sup \{ u : u \in \mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\Sigma, E) \}.

As \Sigma increases, \rho_{\max} decreases. As E decreases, \rho_{\max} decreases. This confirms Design Axiom D1 in the monotone regime.

G.5 CARe vs. Exact HJ

For n=2, exact HJ reachability is tractable and serves as the ground truth. CARe with a neural network approximation achieves \epsilon-close reachable sets with SMT-certified error bounds, demonstrating the viability of the certified approximation approach. The SMT solver certifies that the residual error of the HJ-based loss function is bounded by \epsilon across the domain of interest.

