Appendix H: Standards Mapping Details

H.1 ISO/IEC TR 5469:2024

ISO/IEC TR 5469:2024 provides guidelines on ensuring the functional safety of AI systems. It addresses the unique risks associated with AI, such as unpredictability and lack of transparency, by recommending comprehensive risk assessment and mitigation strategies. The document describes properties, related risk factors, available methods and processes relating to the use of AI inside a safety-related function, the use of non-AI safety-related functions to ensure safety for AI-controlled equipment, and the use of AI systems to design and develop safety-related functions.

H.2 ISO/PAS 8800:2024

ISO/PAS 8800 considers and adapts to road vehicles the general framework described in ISO/IEC TR 5469 on safety properties.

H.3 SEooC (Safety Element out of Context)

For AI SoCs developed as SEooC, the trusted statement must simultaneously specify the certification or evaluation object, covered functions and versions, usage assumptions, external safety mechanisms, and the final evidence scope.

H.4 PAC Mapping Table

PAC Component Standards Mapping Precision
Safety Authority SEooC Developed to ASIL D (ISO 26262) or SIL 3 (IEC 61508), independent from the AI module (QM / unrated)
Perception contracts (P1)–(P3) SOTIF (ISO 21448) + data validation per ISO/IEC TR 5469 Clause 6.3.2 (P1) set-membership = worst-case validation; (P2) conformal = probabilistic validation with coverage guarantee; (P3) MR-CBF = Lipschitz-bounded validation
