H.5 Independence Requirement

The AI module is QM (Quality Management, unrated) under ISO 26262. The safety authority is developed to ASIL D. The independence requirement means the safety authority must be implemented in a separate execution domain (e.g., a separate core or a certified microcontroller) and must not share memory or timing resources with the AI module.

